The 30 s Connected-only fallback stamped activation time from
getCurrentTime() with a possibly zero/stale timeDifference:
Connected is set on the first valid data on a generic connection
(ConnectionsManager.cpp:885) which can precede the handshake that
recomputes timeDifference, and reconnects reuse sessions without a
new handshake. Activation now requires Connected AND a
server-originated round in this process (mayStampActivation), else it
stays PENDING — a late activation is safe, an early one enrols
pre-activation messages.

The round signal itself is hardened: the processUpdateArray hook now
fires only for server-originated batches (fromGetDifference ||
date != 0); locally synthesised batches (cache read-state,
FileRef/Push/SecretChat replays, all (false, 0)) no longer set
roundSeen.

D-08 (audit): onConnectionStateChanged is verified dead (no caller,
no didUpdateConnectionState observer, connectedSeen never read).
It is removed, not wired: with the fallback gone, wiring it would
only call maybeStampPending and stamp nothing. Evidence and the
unexecuted runtime scenarios (clock skew, stale diff, lastServerTime
trap, resumeNetwork correction) are documented in
~/workspace/aligram/phase3-1-r7-note.md. Strict boundary
(date > A) and the edit_date >= asymmetry are unchanged.
